No remaining blocker or serious finding **that could make the screen pass noise or a noisier version**. But I do **not** agree with putting this test to Alex yet: the new rule makes it stop every time.

For example, if the largest difference between the current request’s two groups is 5, the first condition’s self-check asks one of those group differences to be **more than 5**. That cannot happen. The test therefore always reports “not decidable,” even if the revised request is better. This follows from the rule at [lines 173–174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:173) and the first condition at [lines 188–191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:188).

Against round 6:

1. **Explaining what the first condition can prove: partly resolved.** [Lines 192–194](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:192) now state its limit, but the self-check prevents the condition from ever being decided.
2. **Keeping the limit on added errors: resolved.** [Lines 200–202](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:200) retain the production limit and stop if the self-check fails; they no longer widen it afterward.
3. **Same-day production comparison: resolved.** [Lines 181–184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-06-architecture-benchmark/results/results-reading.md:181) send the production reference on the same day.

I agree with the reading: the current split should not be promoted, and the evidence request is a reasonable next target, without claiming that one sentence has been proved to cause the loss. I agree with the recommended direction, but the test needs a workable first-condition self-check before it goes to Alex.

